  title: Mangroves break the waves
  body: Mangrove roots and trunks slow the sea down. Across 500 metres of mangroves,
    wave height can drop by half or more, and each kilometre can lower a storm surge
    by 5 to 50 centimetres. Clearing them leaves the shore open to the waves.
